{"id":"20.09.FindObjects3D","contentHtml":"<blockquote>\n<p>This project was born from an idea <mark>that came to me in a dream</mark>, and became my first deep dive into multiplayer development. It is a prototype of a multiplayer \"hidden object\" game where players compete in speed on a randomly generated level.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>As a <mark>Solo Developer</mark>, I was responsible for everything: from network architecture and generation algorithm to key 3D assets and UI.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The key architectural task was to <mark>create a complex procedural level, identical for all players with minimal network traffic</mark>. The solution is to design a fully <strong>deterministic system</strong> that generates the entire scene from a single synchronized <code>seed</code>.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Procedural Placement:</strong> Implemented a 2D packing algorithm (<code>MaxRectsBinPack</code>) for dense and random placement of multiple 3D objects without intersections.</li>\n<li><strong>Deterministic Synchronization:</strong> To minimize network traffic, <strong>only one <code>seed</code></strong> is synchronized. A deterministic algorithm on each client generates an identical scene from it.</li>\n<li><strong>Multiplayer:</strong> Used Photon for connection, movement synchronization, and <code>seed</code> transfer, as well as for <strong>synchronizing game events</strong> (finding items, changing player scores).</li>\n<li><strong>Assets:</strong> Created key 3D models (room, player head) in <code>Blender</code>, UI, and configured <code>Terrain</code>. Objects for searching are free assets.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Performant Prototype:</strong> Created a scalable multiplayer prototype, successfully tested with friends.</li>\n<li><strong>Effective Architecture:</strong> The deterministic approach allowed synchronizing complex scenes with <strong>minimal possible network traffic</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Key Competency:</strong> The project became my first immersion into <strong>network game architecture and procedural generation</strong>, proving the ability to solve algorithmic problems (<code>2D Bin Packing</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Find Objects 3D","date":"2020-09","type":"project","tagsArray":["Unity","C#","Photoshop","Blender","Multiplayer","PC","Photon"],"heroVideo":["bl_caF45vC8"],"shortDescription":"<p>My first multiplayer project. Implemented a <mark>deterministic placement algorithm</mark> that synchronizes complex levels via a single <code>seed</code>.</p>\n","role":"solo","projectIcon":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/card.mp4?v=1765046984202","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/screenshots/1.webp","width":1920,"height":1080},{"src":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/screenshots/2.webp","width":1920,"height":1080},{"src":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/screenshots/3.webp","width":1920,"height":1080},{"src":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/screenshots/4.webp","width":1920,"height":1080},{"src":"/images/projects/20.09.FindObjects3D/screenshots/5.webp","width":1920,"height":1080}]}